COPY.update({'EuroAfrica provides a clear view of the key commodities and manufactured goods moving between Africa and Europe. From agricultural produce and strategic minerals to machinery, pharmaceuticals and transport equipment, explore the sectors driving commercial exchange across both continents.': 'From agricultural produce and natural resources to machinery and manufactured goods, discover the sectors shaping commercial exchange across both continents.', 'Africa and Europe are connected by established trade relationships spanning agriculture, manufacturing, energy, infrastructure and consumer goods.\n\nAfrican markets supply Europe with valuable agricultural commodities, horticultural produce, minerals and manufactured goods, while European industries provide African markets with machinery, transport equipment, pharmaceuticals, refined products and foodstuffs.\n\nEuroAfrica brings these trade flows together in one accessible platform, helping businesses, professionals and interested stakeholders understand what is traded, where key products originate and the sectors creating commercial opportunities between the two regions.': 'Africa and Europe bring complementary strengths to global trade. Explore the products moving in each direction, the sectors behind them and the commercial links between the two regions.', 'Africa and Europe bring different strengths to international trade.\n\nAfrica combines agricultural capacity, natural resources and expanding manufacturing industries. Europe contributes advanced machinery, transportation systems, pharmaceuticals, industrial products and established manufacturing capabilities.\n\nTogether, these complementary strengths create trade relationships across numerous sectors and markets.\n\nEuroAfrica helps you explore those connections and identify the categories shaping commerce between the two continents.': 'Agricultural capacity, natural resources and expanding manufacturing connect with advanced machinery, industrial products and established supply networks.\n\nExplore how these strengths complement one another, from the origins of a product to its role in a wider market.', "Whether you're researching a particular product category, exploring a market or looking for information about trade between Africa and Europe, you can contact us with your enquiry.\n\nTell us what you're interested in and provide the relevant details. Our team will review your enquiry and respond using the contact information provided.": 'Researching a product, exploring a sector or looking for more information? Share the details of your enquiry. Our team will review your request and respond using the contact information you provide.'})

